content.text:
We can reuse the **main site’s upload method**. I was wrong earlier: the main checkout sends receipts to a Google Apps Script web app first. The service account is only a fallback. :codex-annotation{index="1"}

That Apps Script may run as its owner, letting it save files to her Drive. Google supports that setting; I can’t confirm the current deployment setting or see the script’s source in the repo. ([Apps Script web apps](https://developers.google.com/apps-script/guides/web))

For group-buy, we’d need to update that script to put receipts in the Tindahan subfolder, then point the GB checkout to it. Open the existing script at [script.google.com](https://script.google.com) while signed into her account, and show me its `Code.gs` and **Deploy → Manage deployments** settings. Don’t publish the OAuth app yet.

