+# Tindahan ni Tinapa group-buy receipts
+
+This is a separate Apps Script web app. It only stores GB receipt images in a private Drive folder. It does not call the main PBC Apps Script or write to Google Sheets.
+
+The main `Peptide Babe Receipts` folder is shared with anyone who has its link. A child folder would inherit that access, so this script creates `Tindahan ni Tinapa Group Buy Receipts` at the top level of My Drive instead. It keeps the folder private and adds only the admin-pbc Drive service account as an editor, so admin-pbc can display the receipts.
+
+## One-time setup
+
+1. Open [script.google.com](https://script.google.com/) while signed in as the Drive owner. Create a new standalone project named `Tindahan ni Tinapa GB Receipts`. Do not edit the main PBC Apps Script.
+2. Replace the starter code with `Code.gs` from this folder.
+3. Open **Project Settings → Script properties**. Add these properties:
+
+   - `TINAPA_GB_RECEIPT_SHARED_SECRET`: a private random value with at least 32 characters. Generate one in PowerShell with `node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"`.
+   - `TINAPA_GB_RECEIPT_READER_EMAIL`: `drive-image-proxy@prs-hub-507415.iam.gserviceaccount.com`.
+
+4. Select `setupTindahanGroupBuyReceipts` in the editor and click **Run**. Approve Drive access as the owner. This creates the private GB folder and shares it with the admin-pbc service account. Keep the folder ID from the execution log for reference.
+5. Click **Deploy → New deployment → Web app**. Set **Execute as** to **Me** and access to **Anyone**. The endpoint is protected by the secret from step 3. Copy the deployed URL ending in `/exec`.
+6. In the Vercel project for `admin-pbc`, add these server-only Production and Preview environment variables:
+
+   - `TINAPA_GB_RECEIPT_SCRIPT_URL`: the Apps Script `/exec` URL.
+   - `TINAPA_GB_RECEIPT_SCRIPT_SECRET`: the exact secret from Script Properties.
+
+7. Redeploy admin-pbc. Group-buy checkout uploads receipts through this endpoint. PBC checkout keeps its existing upload path.
+
+Never add the shared secret as a `NEXT_PUBLIC_` variable or paste it into storefront code. If you change the Apps Script deployment, update the Vercel URL and redeploy admin-pbc.
